            {
               "text": "<p><ul class=\"citation\"><li><i><b>Addition Identity:</b> There is a number, zero (0), such that when we add it to any number <b>a</b>, the result is <b>a</b>:<br /> a + 0 = a</i></li></ul></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "We can show this with our hands. When all fingers on the left hand are down, we have zero (0). When we raise fingers on the right hand, we add them to the \"zero\" of the left hand. The result is just the number of fingers raised on the right hand.\n\nTable 1 above shows this idea too, making it easy to understand.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
