      {
         "question": "Can we think of a number sequence as adding 1 to the previous number?",
         "yesNoAnswer": "Yes",
         "additionalInfo": "Yes! We count numbers in order, and each number is 1 more than the one before. So the sequence is made by adding 1 each time to get the next number."
      },
      {
         "question": "Since zero (0) means empty, can we always hide it when it is on the left side?",
         "yesNoAnswer": "Yes",
         "additionalInfo": "Yes! We can leave out zero when it is on the left side of a number. For example, \"01\" is the same as \"1.\" But \"10\" is different—it means something else."
